# Tangerine Compiler — Proof-Carrying Patch (audit §37)
# Self-hosting compiler written in Tangerine
#
# proof_patch.tg assembles ONE audit §37 ProofCarryingPatch report from the
# §31 SemanticDelta (semantic_delta.tg) / §36 ChangeBudget (change_budget.tg)
# machinery: the report bundles the delta itself with the four
# compiler-verified stage flags, the delta's domain row lists (§31 records),
# the §36-rule unsafe-marker rows, the abi / public-api deltas, the item-29
# evidence surfaces (source delta, drop-plan / allocation / obligation /
# coverage / performance rows, affected tests, the §41 equivalence result)
# and the budget envelope's violation list. The module reads ONLY
# SemanticDelta / ChangeBudget / EquivalenceResult /
# VerifiedCompilationEvidence records (never AST / typed /
# MIR state) and mirrors the semantic_delta.tg / change_budget.tg /
# repair_candidates.tg idioms.
#
# CLAIM DISCIPLINE — what "proven" means here. The audit is explicit: "Do
# not call arbitrary application behavior 'proven' — this covers only what
# the compiler/verifiers actually established." A ProofCarryingPatch carries
# (1) a semantic_delta (what the §31 diff recorded between two snapshots),
# (2) a budget_result (what the §36 envelope check decided) and (3) the
# compiler-verified flags parses / resolves / types / ownership — and
# nothing else is ever claimed "proven". In particular:
#   - The four flags reflect the compiler PIPELINE stages only: parses = the
#     source parsed; resolves = name resolution succeeded; types = type
#     checking succeeded; ownership = the access/ownership convention checks
#     succeeded — each for the programs the patch spans. The flags are never
#     inferred here from a delta: every true flag of a patch comes from a
#     VerifiedCompilationEvidence (audit item 20 — the record of the stages
#     a REAL compile ran, assembled by the caller that RAN the stage; an
#     unset flag is an unproven property, never a denied one). The two
#     assemblers map the evidence flags onto the patch's four: parse_ok ->
#     parses, resolution_ok -> resolves, type_ok -> types, and
#     access_ok + resource_ok + mir_verify_ok -> ownership (the ownership
#     flag stands for the whole access/ownership convention + MIR-verify
#     gate). Repair machinery (repair_candidates.tg) is advisory intent and
#     is not part of the record: a patch reports what the compiler
#     established, never what a repair suggests.
#   - The row lists and deltas report what the §31/§36 machinery established
#     (the TYPED row records of the delta domain — audit item 14). No row
#     is invented: the flat lists are projections of existing delta rows,
#     and a surface the delta cannot see stays empty (documented gaps
#     below).
#   - Application behavior (what the patched program DOES at run time) is
#     never a patch's claim. A verified budget says the change fits its
#     allowance envelope; it does not say the change is behaviorally
#     correct.
#
# FOURTH-AUDIT P0-16/P0-17/P0-18 UPDATE. The four booleans above are
# replaced by FOURTEEN typed VerificationStatus fields (Verified / Failed /
# Unavailable), one per stage: parse / resolve / type / access / resource /
# mir-after-lowering / post-mono mir / post-opt mir / effects /
# capabilities-contracts / abi / budget / affected-tests completeness /
# equivalence.
#
# (AUDIT ORDER P0-15) THE VERIFICATION-LEVEL GATE: a patch assembled by
# proof_patch_of_level at ProvisionalFrontEnd / VerifiedFrontend is a
# REFUSAL patch (budget_status + affected-tests Unavailable and a
# "budget:verification-level-unavailable" row), and verified_proof_patch —
# its ONE wrapper constructor — returns None for every level below
# VerifiedFull. A transaction that stopped before final MIR/snapshot
# creation therefore cannot serialize as a VerifiedProofPatch. A flag false for a stage the evidence CAPTURED is Failed; a
# stage the evidence never captured is Unavailable (never a denial); and
# proof_patch_all_verified requires every status Verified — so a route
# without a post-opt-MIR or ABI checkpoint (the snapshot route captures
# neither) can never report complete verification. proof_patch_proven_fields
# renders "<stage>: <status word>" rows. The drop_plan_delta field carries
# the §31 typed DropPlanDelta rows (the persisted resource-checker plan),
# never a sink-convention reconstruction; proof_patch_of_status /
# proof_patch_between refuse with Unavailable when the old snapshot (the
# delta baseline) is missing — budget_result carries a
# "budget:delta-unavailable" row and budget_status is Unavailable instead
# of an empty-delta pass.
#
# (P0 PROOF-GATING) THE CONSTRUCTOR GATE: verified_proof_patch — the ONE
# construction path of VerifiedProofPatch (the fully verified class) —
# requires level == VerifiedFull AND proof_patch_all_verified(patch) (ALL
# fourteen statuses Verified, so no Failed/Unavailable stage can ever ride
# a value typed as a verified proof) AND an AVAILABLE delta, IN THE
# CONSTRUCTOR. Callers holding a weaker-but-honest claim use the distinct
# classes CompilationVerifiedPatch / BudgetVerifiedPatch /
# TestVerifiedPatch (each with its predicate inline in its constructor)
# rather than a partial object named VerifiedProofPatch;
# proof_patch_verified_class_word names the strongest truthful class of a
# patch's statuses.
#
# RECORD-NAME MAPPING (the audit's names onto the §31 records that exist —
# the §29 adaptation discipline, never invented look-alikes):
#   - The audit's EffectDelta / CapabilityDelta rows are semantic_delta.tg's
#     typed records: effect rows are EffectDelta { function, before: and
#     after: EffectSummaryView } (the §11 dirty word + capability-id texts
#     of both sides); capability rows are CapabilityDelta { function,
#     capability, before/after presence }. effect_delta / capability_delta
#     hold those records whole.
#   - ContractDelta / ApiDelta / AbiDelta exist under the audit's names:
#     ContractDelta rows carry the clause's StableContractId stable key
#     with the before/after ContractSemantic projections; ApiDelta /
#     AbiDelta (the changed flag + symmetric-difference rows) are REBUILT
#     from the delta's typed AbiDeltaView surfaces in proof_patch_of_delta
#     (semantic_delta.tg's public_api_delta / abi_delta fields carry the
#     full before/after row views; the patch's §37 report shape keeps the
#     changed-flag + rows form).
#   - unsafe_delta holds TEXT rows (the §36 counting rule's marker rows —
#     the audit's marker vocabulary), derived from the delta's TYPED
#     UnsafeFact rows (audit item 16): every CREATED fact of
#     delta.unsafe_delta renders as "<function> <kind-word>[:<site>]"
#     (semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text — the snapshot marker vocabulary
#     "unsafe-fn" / "extern-call:<name>" / "transmute" /
#     "unknown-call:<name>"). The ownership-row counting rule is gone.
#   - affected_tests / uncovered_new_paths are Vec[String] extension
#     surfaces the audit names but SemanticDelta carries no test or coverage
#     rows for (tests/coverage carry no rows today — documented in
#     semantic_delta.tg): affected_tests is filled from the caller's
#     PatchEvidenceBundle (a consumer holding the semantic-index test
#     relationships — semantic_index.tg — supplies it), uncovered_new_paths
#     stays empty until a coverage consumer fills it, and the item-29
#     coverage_delta / performance_delta surfaces are the same kind of
#     caller-fed row list. The module never synthesizes a test or a path
#     name from an affected key.
#
# EVIDENCE SURFACES (third audit item 29): beyond the §31-derived rows the
# patch carries first-class evidence surfaces the delta cannot see, all
# defaulted so every pre-item-29 construction site stays valid:
#   source_delta — the caller's source-level diff (changed files + hunk
#     hashes). EMPTY by default; filled only from
#     PatchEvidenceBundle.source_delta when the caller holds the diff.
#   drop_plan_delta — per (function, place) drop-plan rows derived from the
#     delta's TYPED OwnershipDelta state words: a row
#     "drop-plan <function> <place> <before> -> <after>" (each side the
#     sorted convention words, "" as "absent") is emitted ONLY where the
#     before/after words show the sink (consume) convention — the ONE
#     convention word with drop semantics (sink transfers ownership into
#     the callee, which finalizes the value if still live). A place whose
#     conventions are let/inout/set churn carries no drop plan and emits
#     nothing; the §31 row carries CONVENTIONS, not a materialized drop
#     schedule — a full drop plan (per-path drop points / drop glue) needs
#     the resource checker's finalize-plan machinery, which a
#     SemanticDelta does not carry (the exact prerequisite for richer
#     rows). The list is typed-empty otherwise, never invented.
#   obligation_results — the trait obligations the caller checked, with
#     status (verbatim caller rows from PatchEvidenceBundle).
#   allocation_delta — the delta's newly-alloc-class effect rows
#     ("<fn-key> alloc <before-bits> -> <after-bits>", the §11 alloc bit —
#     the exact rows the §36 check-8 count consumes) plus the budget's
#     RESERVED allocation byte cap and the used-bytes total. used_bytes is
#     ALWAYS None today: the §11 effect view carries bits + capability ids
#     and no allocation byte count, so no bytes-used value is derivable
#     (the same byte-payload prerequisite budget check 8 reports); the
#     caller's extra rows append after the derived rows.
#   coverage_delta / performance_delta — caller-fed row surfaces (empty
#     until a coverage ingest / perf run supplies them).
#   equivalence — the §41 EquivalenceResult for the change, when the caller
#     holds one (PatchEvidenceBundle.equivalence). The §36 refactor gate
#     (item 32) consumes it: budget_result carries a
#     "budget:equivalence-required" row when the budget declares an
#     equivalence requirement (EquivalenceRequirement) and this result is
#     missing or insufficient. Option::None = no result held, never an
#     implicit claim.
#
# FLAT-LIST DERIVATION (proof_patch_of_delta, over ONE delta + ONE budget +
# ONE evidence record + ONE optional evidence bundle — the module doc's
# numbered checks):
#   1. contract_delta := the delta's contract rows (§31 ContractDelta).
#   2. effect_delta := the delta's effect rows (§31 EffectDelta — the
#      before/after §11 views).
#   3. capability_delta := the delta's capability rows (§31 CapabilityDelta
#      — presence before/after).
#   4. unsafe_delta := the marker rows of the §36 EXACT COUNTING RULE
#      (change_budget.tg check 7 — audit item 16): the CREATED facts of
#      delta.unsafe_delta rendered as "<function> <kind-word>[:<site>]"
#      (semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text), in the delta's own sorted row
#      order.
#   5. abi_delta / public_api_delta := rebuilt from the delta's typed
#      AbiDeltaView surfaces: the changed flag = the before/after row sets
#      differ (semantic_delta_rows_same), the rows = their symmetric
#      difference (semantic_delta_rows_diff).
#   6. budget_result := budget_verify_with_equivalence(budget, delta,
#      bundle.equivalence) — the "budget:" violation lines; empty = the
#      delta verifies within the budget envelope AND the budget's item-32
#      equivalence requirement, when one is declared, holds. That is the
#      ONLY "budget verified" claim the patch makes.
#   7. The fourteen typed stage statuses := the evidence mapping of the ONE
#      evidence record (see CLAIM DISCIPLINE + the P0-16 note); the item-29
#      evidence surfaces come from the bundle (a defaulted
#      PatchEvidenceBundle {} leaves them empty).
#   8. drop_plan_delta := the §31 delta's typed DropPlanDelta rows
#      (delta.drop_plan_delta — the persisted resource-checker plan).
#   9. allocation_delta := the delta's newly-alloc-class effect rows + the
#      budget's reserved byte cap (used_bytes None — see EVIDENCE
#      SURFACES).
#
# SPAN FORM (proof_patch_between — the CHANGE patch, over the OLD and NEW
# evidence records of the two compilations a change spans): the flags are
# the SAME evidence mapping ANDed across BOTH records — parses :=
# old.parse_ok && new.parse_ok (and so on for resolves / types / ownership,
# ownership over the three evidence flags of each side). A stage property
# is claimed only when BOTH compilations the patch spans established it
# (one unverified endpoint leaves the property unproven for the span —
# claim discipline). The optional old_delta is the §31 diff the caller
# computed between the two compilations' finalized states (semantic_delta_of
# over their sessions' snapshots); when it is NOT supplied the report's
# delta stays the empty delta (which verifies against ANY budget) with the
# flags still set from the evidence, and the caller fills the real delta by
# re-running proof_patch_of_delta with it (the flags then ride the same
# evidence-driven mapping). The between-form never fabricates a delta. The
# item-29 evidence bundle is the same defaulted optional parameter as in
# proof_patch_of_delta.
#
# EMPTY-DEFAULT: proof_patch_new() is the claim-nothing patch — the empty
# §31 delta (which verifies against ANY budget: an empty delta carries no
# keys, no rows and no counts), every flag false, every list / evidence
# surface empty (empty SourceDelta / AllocationDelta, no equivalence
# result). All Vec / evidence fields are defaulted so a patch can be
# assembled incrementally: rows push
# onto the lists and flags are set as the pipeline stages establish them.
# Re-running proof_patch_of_delta over the patch's semantic_delta re-derives
# the report lists from a delta + budget and sets the flags from the
# evidence record the caller supplies.
#
# ANCHORS:
#   ProofCarryingPatch        — the §37 protocol record (the audit's struct,
#                               field for field + the item-29 evidence
#                               surfaces).
#   SourceDelta               — the item-29 source-level delta (changed
#                               files + hunk hashes; defaulted empty).
#   AllocationDelta           — the item-29 allocation evidence delta (alloc
#                               rows + the optional byte totals; used_bytes
#                               None under the byte-payload prerequisite).
#   PatchEvidenceBundle       — the item-29 optional caller evidence bundle
#                               (every field defaulted; assemblers accept
#                               it as the defaulted last parameter).
#                               (audit item 9) its optional `affected`
#                               AffectedResult carries the affected
#                               closure's shared CompletenessInfo onto the
#                               patch's analysis_completeness rows.
#   VerifiedCompilationEvidence — audit item 20's record of what ONE real
#                               compilation's pipeline stages established
#                               (revision + the ten stage flags).
#   verified_compilation_evidence — the ONE documented constructor of the
#                               evidence record (revision + ten named stage
#                               flags, each documented below).
#   evidence_all_ok           — the predicate: every stage flag is true.
#   proof_patch_new           — the empty / claim-nothing patch.
#   proof_patch_of_delta      — the assembly convenience (delta + budget +
#                               evidence + optional evidence bundle ->
#                               report; the derivation steps 1-9 above;
#                               flags from the ONE evidence).
#   proof_patch_between       — the SPAN assembly (old + new evidence +
#                               budget + optional §31 delta + optional
#                               evidence bundle -> report; flags ANDed
#                               across both evidence records).
#   proof_patch_with_evidence — the bundle application (copies the caller
#                               surfaces onto an assembled patch).
#   VerificationLevel         — ProvisionalFrontEnd | VerifiedFrontend |
#                               VerifiedFull (audit order P0-15).
#   proof_patch_of_level      — the level-gated assembly: VerifiedFull
#                               assembles like proof_patch_of_status; every
#                               weaker level refuses.
#   VerifiedProofPatch        — the fully verified class (the audit's
#                               FullyVerifiedPatch: level + patch + proof
#                               hash); verified_proof_patch is its ONE
#                               constructor and requires VerifiedFull +
#                               proof_patch_all_verified + an available
#                               delta in the constructor itself.
#   CompilationVerifiedPatch /
#   BudgetVerifiedPatch /
#   TestVerifiedPatch         — the truthful weaker classes (compiler
#                               stages / + budget / + tests+equivalence),
#                               each gated in its own constructor.
#   proof_patch_verified_class_word — the strongest truthful class word of
#                               a patch's fourteen statuses.
#   proof_drop_plan_rows      — the item-29 drop-plan derivation (sink-
#                               bearing ownership rows; exact row grammar
#                               above).
#   proof_allocation_delta    — the item-29 allocation derivation (alloc-
#                               class effect rows + the budget byte cap).
#   proof_patch_proven_fields — the true-flag name list (the claim surface:
#                               parses / resolves / types / ownership only,
#                               fixed pipeline order).
#   proof_patch_lane_check    — the item-29 unit-style lane rows.
#   unsafe markers            — "<function> <kind-word>[:<site>]" fact row
#                               texts (the §36 counting rule's rows).

use tg_compiler::ids::{StableDigest, stable_digest_of}
use tg_compiler::semantic_delta::{
  SemanticDelta, ContractDelta, EffectDelta, CapabilityDelta, OwnershipDelta, ApiDelta, AbiDelta,
  EffectSummaryView, DropPlanDelta, DropSiteDelta,
  semantic_delta_empty, semantic_delta_rows_same, semantic_delta_rows_diff,
  semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text,
  # (audit item 9) the affected closure's verdict + the shared completeness
  # render the patch's analysis row carries.
  AffectedResult,
  DeltaStatus
}
use tg_compiler::semantic_model::{CompletenessInfo, completeness_info_subset, completeness_info_render}
use tg_compiler::change_budget::{
  ChangeBudget, budget_verify_with_equivalence, budget_refactor_default,
  budget_refactor_with_level
}
use tg_compiler::equivalence::{
  EquivalenceLevel, EquivalenceResult, equivalence_result_is_proven,
  equivalence_structural, equivalence_proven_finite, equivalence_tested
}

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The §37 protocol record + the item-29 evidence bundle
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

# ONE source-level delta (third audit item 29): the changed source files
# and the content hashes of the hunks the caller's source diff recorded.
# The §31 SemanticDelta is the semantic authority; this surface carries
# the caller's source-level evidence alongside it. Every field defaults
# empty, so a patch assembled without source information stays valid (the
# source_delta of a ProofCarryingPatch is SourceDelta {} until a caller
# supplies one through PatchEvidenceBundle).
struct SourceDelta
  # The changed source file paths (the caller's diff order).
  changed_files: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  # The content hashes of the changed hunks (the caller's diff order).
  hunk_hashes: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
end

# ONE allocation evidence delta (third audit item 29): the delta's
# newly-alloc-class effect rows (the §11 alloc bit, the exact rows the §36
# check-8 count consumes) plus the optional BYTE totals of the budget's
# allocation surface. budget_bytes is the budget's RESERVED
# allocation_budget_bytes cap (None = the budget declares none); used_bytes
# is the allocation bytes the change USED — ALWAYS None today, with the
# exact prerequisite stated: the §11 effect view a SemanticDelta carries
# holds bits + capability ids and NO allocation byte count, so no
# bytes-used value is derivable (the same gap budget check 8's
# allocation-bytes row reports; a future byte-carrying effect payload plugs
# in here and at that check).
struct AllocationDelta
  # "<fn-key> alloc <before-bits> -> <after-bits>" rows, delta row order.
  rows: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  # The budget's reserved allocation byte cap, when it declares one.
  budget_bytes: Option[Int] = Option::None
  # The allocation bytes used — underivable from a SemanticDelta today (the
  # byte-payload prerequisite above); always None until that payload lands.
  used_bytes: Option[Int] = Option::None
end

# ONE optional evidence bundle (third audit item 29): the caller-supplied
# evidence surfaces a §31 SemanticDelta cannot carry. Every field is
# defaulted, so the assemblers accept a bundle only when a caller holds
# one — an omitted bundle is PatchEvidenceBundle {} and every patch
# surface defaulted. The bundle is EVIDENCE, never a claim: the assemblers
# copy its rows onto the patch verbatim (the claim discipline of the
# module doc) and the §36 equivalence gate consumes only `equivalence`.
#   source_delta — the source-level diff (SourceDelta; None = no source
#                  information supplied).
#   obligation_results — the trait obligations the caller checked, with
#                  their status (caller text rows, "obligation: status").
#   allocation_delta_rows — caller-supplied allocation rows (appended to
#                  the delta-derived alloc-class rows; measured rows,
#                  profiler output — the caller's order).
#   affected_tests — the tests the change affects (the semantic-index /
#                  test-relationship consumer fills it).
#   coverage_delta_rows — the coverage rows a coverage ingest established
#                  (empty until such an ingest feeds them).
#   performance_delta_rows — the performance facts a perf run established
#                  (empty until one feeds them).
#   equivalence — the §41 EquivalenceResult the §36 refactor-equivalence
#                  requirement (equivalence_requirement, third audit item
#                  32) consumes; Option::None = no result held (the gate
#                  reports the missing result when the budget demands one).
struct PatchEvidenceBundle
  source_delta: Option[SourceDelta] = Option::None
  obligation_results: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  allocation_delta_rows: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  affected_tests: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  coverage_delta_rows: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  performance_delta_rows: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  equivalence: Option[EquivalenceResult] = Option::None
  # (audit item 9) the affected closure the change was verified over, when
  # the caller computed one: its shared CompletenessInfo (class / reason /
  # counts / analysis model) is attached to the patch's
  # analysis_completeness rows so a consumer sees HOW COMPLETE the
  # analysis behind the patch's claims was.
  affected: Option[AffectedResult] = Option::None
end

# (fourth-audit P0-16) THE TYPED VERIFICATION STATUS. Every verification
# surface of a patch is ONE of:
#   Verified    — the stage ran and established the property (evidence flag
#                 true, or the assembly derived the property from proved
#                 data: e.g. an empty budget_result).
#   Failed      — the stage ran and did NOT establish the property (a false
#                 evidence flag whose stage the evidence captured; a
#                 non-empty budget result; an equivalence result that is
#                 not a proof).
#   Unavailable — the stage was not captured / cannot be decided from the
#                 evidence at hand (a false flag whose stage the evidence
#                 does NOT capture; a missing equivalence result; a missing
#                 old snapshot for the delta; a budget assembled over an
#                 unavailable delta). Unavailable is NEVER a denial and
#                 NEVER counts as complete verification.
pub enum VerificationStatus
  Verified
  Failed
  Unavailable
end

# The canonical word of a verification status (the proven-field renderer /
# the verification rows).
pub def verification_status_word(s: VerificationStatus) -> String
  match s
  when VerificationStatus::Verified then "verified"
  when VerificationStatus::Failed then "failed"
  when VerificationStatus::Unavailable then "unavailable"
  end
end

# Whether the status is Verified — the ONLY status an "all verified"
# predicate accepts (not merely not-failed).
pub def verification_status_is_verified(s: VerificationStatus) -> Bool
  match s
  when VerificationStatus::Verified then true
  when _ then false
  end
end

# The names of the ten captured evidence stages, in pipeline order (the
# default captured set of verified_compilation_evidence: a caller naming
# all ten flags asserts all ten stages were run — a false flag is then
# Failed, never Unavailable).
pub def verification_stage_names_all() -> Vec[String]
  Vec::from([
    "parse".to_string(),
    "resolve".to_string(),
    "type".to_string(),
    "access".to_string(),
    "resource".to_string(),
    "mir".to_string(),
    "post-mono-mir".to_string(),
    "post-opt-mir".to_string(),
    "effects".to_string(),
    "capabilities".to_string(),
    "abi".to_string()
  ])
end

# The captured stage names of the driver's snapshot route (fourth-audit
# P0-16, mirroring the driver's capture doc): the stages THAT route's
# pipeline actually runs. Since audit order item 7 the route runs the
# REAL post-lowering ABI verifier (driver_abi_verify_rows), so "abi" IS
# captured and a false abi_verify_ok is Failed, never Unavailable.
# (the shared finalized-MIR pipeline) The route now compiles through
# finalize.tg's finalize_verified_mir, which runs the UNCONDITIONAL
# post-mono verify_mir checkpoint — "post-mono-mir" IS captured too, so
# the captured set is the FULL stage vocabulary (a false mono flag is
# Failed, never Unavailable) and no route sets a false placeholder.
pub def verification_stage_names_driver_route() -> Vec[String]
  Vec::from([
    "parse".to_string(),
    "resolve".to_string(),
    "type".to_string(),
    "access".to_string(),
    "resource".to_string(),
    "mir".to_string(),
    "post-mono-mir".to_string(),
    "post-opt-mir".to_string(),
    "effects".to_string(),
    "capabilities".to_string(),
    "abi".to_string()
  ])
end

# ONE §37 report: the §31 delta carried whole, the compiler-verified stage
# flags, the delta's domain row lists, the abi / public-api deltas, the
# item-29 evidence surfaces, the §36 budget verdict and the §41
# equivalence result the item-32 refactor gate consumes. Every Vec /
# evidence field is defaulted so the patch can be assembled incrementally
# (see the module doc); semantic_delta / abi_delta / public_api_delta have
# no default and must be named on construction (proof_patch_new supplies
# the empty forms).
struct ProofCarryingPatch
  # The §31 semantic delta itself — the diff this patch reports. When the
  # delta was UNAVAILABLE (a missing old snapshot), this stays the empty
  # delta with delta_unavailable carrying the reason; budget_result then
  # REFUSES (a "budget:delta-unavailable" row) and budget_status is
  # Unavailable (fourth-audit P0-18: never an empty delta plus a passing
  # budget).
  semantic_delta: SemanticDelta
  # (fourth-audit P0-18) The delta's unavailability reason; None = the
  # delta was computed (Complete).
  delta_unavailable: Option[String] = Option::None
  # (fourth-audit P0-16) THE TYPED VERIFICATION STATUSES, one per stage,
  # exposed SEPARATELY (never collapsed into one flag): each is
  # Verified / Failed / Unavailable (see VerificationStatus). A patch can
  # NEVER report complete verification (proof_patch_all_verified) while
  # post-opt MIR or ABI is Unavailable.
  parse_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  resolve_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  type_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  access_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  resource_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  # mir-after-lowering: the MIR verifier accepted the lowered program.
  mir_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  # post-mono mir: the verifier accepted the monomorphized program.
  post_mono_mir_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  # post-opt mir: the verifier accepted the optimized program (the final
  # boundary before codegen).
  post_opt_mir_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  # effects: the §11 effect-class annotation check.
  effects_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  # capabilities/contracts: the capability/contract verification surface.
  capabilities_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  # abi: the ABI/export surface check.
  abi_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  # budget: the §36 envelope verdict (Verified = the budget_result is
  # empty; Failed = violations; Unavailable = no complete delta to check).
  budget_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  # affected-tests completeness: Verified = the caller supplied the
  # affected tests or the delta has nothing to enumerate; Unavailable = the
  # delta affects entities but no test rows were supplied.
  affected_tests_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  # equivalence: the §41 result status (Verified = a PROVEN result; Failed
  # = an unproven result; Unavailable = no result held).
  equivalence_status: VerificationStatus = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  # The delta's contract rows (§31 ContractDelta — before/after semantic
  # projections under the clause's StableContractId).
  contract_delta: Vec[ContractDelta] = Vec::new()
  # The delta's effect rows (§31 EffectDelta — before/after §11 views).
  effect_delta: Vec[EffectDelta] = Vec::new()
  # The delta's capability rows (§31 CapabilityDelta — before/after
  # presence).
  capability_delta: Vec[CapabilityDelta] = Vec::new()
  # The §36-rule unsafe-marker rows ("<function> <kind-word>[:<site>]" —
  # the created UnsafeFact rows of delta.unsafe_delta; the module doc's
  # derivation step 4).
  unsafe_delta: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  # The ABI surface delta (changed flag + symmetric-difference rows —
  # rebuilt from the delta's typed AbiDeltaView surface).
  abi_delta: AbiDelta
  # The public-API surface delta (rebuilt the same way).
  public_api_delta: ApiDelta
  # (third audit item 29) The source-level delta — evidence-only, defaulted
  # empty, filled from PatchEvidenceBundle.source_delta when supplied.
  source_delta: SourceDelta = SourceDelta {}
  # (third audit item 29; fourth-audit P0-17) The typed per (function,
  # place) DropPlanDelta rows the §31 diff produced (delta.drop_plan_delta)
  # — the resource checker's persisted, materialized drop plan; NOT a
  # reconstruction from ownership/sink convention rows.
  drop_plan_delta: Vec[DropPlanDelta] = Vec::new()
  # (third audit item 29) The trait obligations the caller checked, with
  # their status (caller text rows — PatchEvidenceBundle.obligation_results).
  obligation_results: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  # (third audit item 29) The allocation evidence delta (derivation step 9
  # plus the caller's extra rows and the budget's byte cap).
  allocation_delta: AllocationDelta = AllocationDelta {}
  # The tests the patch affects — an extension surface (no §31 test rows
  # today; a consumer holding the index/test relationships fills it through
  # PatchEvidenceBundle.affected_tests).
  affected_tests: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  # (third audit item 29) The coverage rows a coverage ingest established —
  # an extension surface, empty until the ingest feeds it
  # (PatchEvidenceBundle.coverage_delta_rows).
  coverage_delta: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  # (third audit item 29) The performance rows a perf run established — an
  # extension surface, empty until one feeds it
  # (PatchEvidenceBundle.performance_delta_rows).
  performance_delta: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  # The newly uncovered paths — an extension surface (no §31 coverage rows
  # today; a consumer holding the coverage machinery fills it).
  uncovered_new_paths: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  # (third audit item 29/32) The §41 EquivalenceResult for the change — the
  # refactor-gating evidence. Option::None = no result held; when the
  # budget declares an equivalence requirement, budget_result carries the
  # "budget:equivalence-required" row unless this result satisfies it
  # (change_budget.budget_verify_with_equivalence, derivation step 6).
  equivalence: Option[EquivalenceResult] = Option::None
  # The §36 envelope verdict: budget_verify_with_equivalence(budget, delta,
  # equivalence)'s output lines (empty = the delta verifies within the
  # budget envelope AND the budget's equivalence requirement, when one is
  # declared, holds).
  budget_result: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  # (audit item 9) The completeness of every analysis underlying the
  # patch's claims, as canonical render rows (completeness_info_render:
  # "<model>|<class>|visited=<n>|returned=<n>|omitted=<n>|<reason>").
  # Filled from PatchEvidenceBundle.affected when the caller computed the
  # affected closure (the closure's CompletenessInfo rides here); EMPTY
  # otherwise — no analysis claim is invented.
  analysis_completeness: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
end

# The empty / claim-nothing patch: the empty §31 delta (which verifies
# against ANY budget), every status Unavailable (no stage is claimed — and
# none is denied), no rows, no violations.
# proof_patch_proven_fields over it is empty — nothing is claimed.
pub def proof_patch_new() -> ProofCarryingPatch
  ProofCarryingPatch {
    semantic_delta: semantic_delta_empty(),
    abi_delta: AbiDelta {
      abi_changed: false
    },
    public_api_delta: ApiDelta {
      public_api_changed: false
    }
  }
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The verification-evidence record (audit item 20)
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# ONE VerifiedCompilationEvidence records what ONE REAL compilation's
# pipeline stages established — the evidence the patch flags come from
# (see CLAIM DISCIPLINE). revision is the content-addressed revision text
# of the program the evidence covers (the revision render of its
# finalized state — semantic_digest_render's "hi-lo" text of the final
# snapshot's digest; "" = not yet bound). The ten stage flags default
# false and have NO other sanctioned constructor: verified_compilation_
# evidence is the ONE public assembly path, and every flag is set only by
# naming it there with the stage meaning the constructor documents — a
# record literal can never claim a stage (an unset flag is an unproven
# property, never a denied one). The stage vocabulary, in pipeline order:
#   parse_ok             — the source parsed (lexer + parser success).
#   resolution_ok        — name resolution succeeded over the parsed tree.
#   type_ok              — type checking succeeded (the typed program is
#                          the type checker's output).
#   access_ok            — the access/ownership convention checker found
#                          no violations (access_check.tg).
#   resource_ok          — the resource checker found no violations
#                          (resource_check.tg).
#   mir_verify_ok        — the MIR verifier accepted the lowered program
#                          (verify_mir at the lowering boundary).
#   mono_verify_ok       — monomorphization completed and its verification
#                          checkpoint passed (the verifier over the
#                          monomorphized program).
#   post_opt_mir_verify_ok — the MIR verifier accepted the OPTIMIZED
#                          program (the final boundary before codegen).
#   effect_verify_ok     — the §11 effect-class annotation check passed
#                          over the lowered MIR
#                          (check_effect_class_annotations_mir).
#   abi_verify_ok        — the ABI/export surface check passed (the
#                          pub/extern surface the abi machinery audits).
# The evidence record itself makes no patch claim: the ASSEMBLERS below
# map the flags onto the patch's four (parse_ok -> parses, resolution_ok
# -> resolves, type_ok -> types, access_ok + resource_ok + mir_verify_ok
# -> ownership). mono_verify_ok / post_opt_mir_verify_ok /
# effect_verify_ok / abi_verify_ok have no patch-flag counterpart — they
# ride the record for the evidence_all_ok gate and for consumers that
# hold a real pipeline.
struct VerifiedCompilationEvidence
  # The revision text of the program this evidence covers ("" = not yet
  # bound).
  revision: String = ""
  # parse_ok: the source parsed (lexer + parser success).
  parse_ok: Bool = false
  # resolution_ok: name resolution succeeded over the parsed tree.
  resolution_ok: Bool = false
  # type_ok: type checking succeeded.
  type_ok: Bool = false
  # access_ok: the access/ownership convention checker found no
  # violations.
  access_ok: Bool = false
  # resource_ok: the resource checker found no violations.
  resource_ok: Bool = false
  # mir_verify_ok: the MIR verifier accepted the lowered program.
  mir_verify_ok: Bool = false
  # mono_verify_ok: monomorphization completed and its verification
  # checkpoint passed.
  mono_verify_ok: Bool = false
  # post_opt_mir_verify_ok: the MIR verifier accepted the optimized
  # program (the final boundary before codegen).
  post_opt_mir_verify_ok: Bool = false
  # effect_verify_ok: the §11 effect-class annotation check passed over
  # the lowered MIR.
  effect_verify_ok: Bool = false
  # abi_verify_ok: the ABI/export surface check passed.
  abi_verify_ok: Bool = false
  # capability_contract_ok: the capability/contract verification surface
  # passed (the contract obligations + capability propagation the checker
  # establishes).
  capability_contract_ok: Bool = false
  # (fourth-audit P0-16) The stage names THIS evidence captured — the
  # stages the producing pipeline actually ran/could run. A false flag for
  # a CAPTURED stage maps to Failed; a false flag for an UNCAPTURED stage
  # maps to Unavailable (never a denial). Defaulted empty: a literal
  # evidence record captures nothing and every false flag is Unavailable.
  stages: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
end

# The ONE documented constructor of a VerifiedCompilationEvidence (see the
# record doc for the stage meanings). revision is the content-addressed
# revision text of the program the stages verified; every flag is a named
# parameter whose meaning the record doc states — a caller sets a flag
# true ONLY for a stage the compiler actually ran to success, and sets the
# flags in the pipeline order below. The record is otherwise claim-nothing:
# every flag the caller does not name stays false. Naming this constructor
# asserts the WHOLE documented pipeline was captured (the default captured
# stage set) — a false flag is then Failed, never Unavailable; a route
# that runs fewer stages must use verified_compilation_evidence_stages
# with its real captured set (fourth-audit P0-16).
pub def verified_compilation_evidence(
  revision: String,
  parse: Bool,
  resolution: Bool,
  types: Bool,
  access: Bool,
  resource: Bool,
  mir: Bool,
  mono: Bool,
  post_opt: Bool,
  effects: Bool,
  abi: Bool,
  capability_contract: Bool = false
) -> VerifiedCompilationEvidence
  verified_compilation_evidence_stages(revision, parse, resolution, types, access,
    resource, mir, mono, post_opt, effects, abi, capability_contract,
    verification_stage_names_all())
end

# The captured-set constructor (fourth-audit P0-16): identical flags plus
# the EXPLICIT list of stage names the producing pipeline captured. The
# stage-name vocabulary is verification_stage_names_all's ("parse",
# "resolve", "type", "access", "resource", "mir", "post-mono-mir",
# "post-opt-mir", "effects", "capabilities", "abi").
pub def verified_compilation_evidence_stages(
  revision: String,
  parse: Bool,
  resolution: Bool,
  types: Bool,
  access: Bool,
  resource: Bool,
  mir: Bool,
  mono: Bool,
  post_opt: Bool,
  effects: Bool,
  abi: Bool,
  capability_contract: Bool,
  stages: Vec[String]
) -> VerifiedCompilationEvidence
  VerifiedCompilationEvidence {
    revision: revision,
    parse_ok: parse,
    resolution_ok: resolution,
    type_ok: types,
    access_ok: access,
    resource_ok: resource,
    mir_verify_ok: mir,
    mono_verify_ok: mono,
    post_opt_mir_verify_ok: post_opt,
    effect_verify_ok: effects,
    abi_verify_ok: abi,
    capability_contract_ok: capability_contract,
    stages: stages
  }
end

# Whether the evidence captured a stage name.
pub def evidence_stage_available(evidence: VerifiedCompilationEvidence, stage: String) -> Bool
  evidence.stages.contains(&stage)
end

# The evidence_all_ok predicate: every one of the stage flags is true
# — the evidence describes a compilation that ran the WHOLE documented
# pipeline to success (parse through the abi + capability/contract
# surfaces). Any false flag means the corresponding stage property is
# unproven (never denied).
pub def evidence_all_ok(evidence: VerifiedCompilationEvidence) -> Bool
  evidence.parse_ok && evidence.resolution_ok && evidence.type_ok &&
    evidence.access_ok && evidence.resource_ok && evidence.mir_verify_ok &&
    evidence.mono_verify_ok && evidence.post_opt_mir_verify_ok &&
    evidence.effect_verify_ok && evidence.abi_verify_ok &&
    evidence.capability_contract_ok
end

# (fourth-audit P0-16) The flag -> status mapping of ONE evidence stage:
# true -> Verified; false -> Failed when the evidence captured the stage
# (the pipeline ran it and it did not establish the property), Unavailable
# when the stage was never captured (the pipeline could not run it — never
# a denial).
pub def proof_evidence_status(
  evidence: VerifiedCompilationEvidence,
  stage: String,
  flag: Bool
) -> VerificationStatus
  if flag then
    VerificationStatus::Verified
  elsif evidence_stage_available(evidence, stage) then
    VerificationStatus::Failed
  else
    VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  end
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# THE ASSEMBLY — ONE ProofCarryingPatch from ONE delta + ONE budget
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The shared derived-row record: the report's §31 flat lists + the abi /
# public-api rebuilt records + the item-29 delta-derived evidence rows
# (drop plans, allocation) + the §36 budget verdict, derived from ONE
# delta + ONE budget + the change's optional §41 equivalence result (the
# module doc's numbered steps 1-9). The two assemblers
# (proof_patch_of_delta / proof_patch_between) differ only in the
# stage-flag derivation (step 7); the rows are always the same function of
# the delta (the equivalence result participates ONLY in the §36 gate,
# step 6).
struct ProofCarryingPatchRows
  contract_delta: Vec[ContractDelta] = Vec::new()
  effect_delta: Vec[EffectDelta] = Vec::new()
  capability_delta: Vec[CapabilityDelta] = Vec::new()
  unsafe_delta: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  abi_delta: AbiDelta
  public_api_delta: ApiDelta
  # (fourth-audit P0-17) the typed drop-plan diff rows carried whole.
  drop_plan_delta: Vec[DropPlanDelta] = Vec::new()
  allocation_delta: AllocationDelta = AllocationDelta {}
  budget_result: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
end

def proof_patch_rows_of(
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  delta: SemanticDelta,
  equivalence: Option[EquivalenceResult]
) -> ProofCarryingPatchRows
  let violations = budget_verify_with_equivalence(&budget, &delta, equivalence)
  let contract_rows = delta.contract_delta.clone()
  let effect_rows = delta.effect_delta.clone()
  let capability_rows = delta.capability_delta.clone()
  let unsafe_rows = proof_unsafe_rows(&delta)
  # (fourth-audit P0-17) the drop-plan rows ARE the §31 typed diff rows —
  # the sink-row reconstruction is gone.
  let drop_rows = delta.drop_plan_delta.clone()
  let allocation = proof_allocation_delta(&budget, &delta)
  let api_changed = !semantic_delta_rows_same(&delta.public_api_delta.before.rows,
    &delta.public_api_delta.after.rows)
  let api_rows = semantic_delta_rows_diff(&delta.public_api_delta.before.rows,
    &delta.public_api_delta.after.rows)
  let abi_changed = !semantic_delta_rows_same(&delta.abi_delta.before.rows,
    &delta.abi_delta.after.rows)
  let abi_rows = semantic_delta_rows_diff(&delta.abi_delta.before.rows,
    &delta.abi_delta.after.rows)
  ProofCarryingPatchRows {
    contract_delta: contract_rows,
    effect_delta: effect_rows,
    capability_delta: capability_rows,
    unsafe_delta: unsafe_rows,
    abi_delta: AbiDelta {
      abi_changed: abi_changed,
      abi_rows: abi_rows
    },
    public_api_delta: ApiDelta {
      public_api_changed: api_changed,
      public_api_rows: api_rows
    },
    drop_plan_delta: drop_rows,
    allocation_delta: allocation,
    budget_result: violations
  }
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The item-29 derived evidence rows
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Whether an ownership state word carries the sink (consume) convention —
# the ONE convention word with drop semantics: sink transfers ownership
# into the callee, which finalizes the value if still live (the parameter
# model's own words). An OwnershipDelta state word is the ";"-joined sorted
# convention-word list of the (function, place) pair ("" = the place row
# did not exist on that side).
def proof_own_word_has_sink(word: String) -> Bool
  for part in word.split(";") do
    if part == "sink" then
      return true
    end
  end
  false
end

# The state-word render of a drop-plan row ("" = the side carried no row).
def proof_drop_state_text(word: String) -> String
  if word.len() == 0 then "absent" else word.clone() end
end

# The drop-plan row of ONE ownership delta:
#   "drop-plan <function> <place> <before> -> <after>"
# with each side rendering the sorted convention words ("" as "absent").
def proof_drop_plan_row_text(row: OwnershipDelta) -> String
  "drop-plan " + row.function.clone() + " " + row.place.clone() + " " +
    proof_drop_state_text(&row.before) + " -> " + proof_drop_state_text(&row.after)
end

# The drop-plan rows of a delta (derivation step 8): one row per TYPED
# OwnershipDelta whose before/after state words show the sink (consume)
# convention on a side — the consume/drop-relevant transitions ONLY. A
# place whose conventions are let/inout/set churn carries no drop plan, so
# it emits nothing; and the §31 ownership row carries access CONVENTIONS,
# not a materialized drop schedule, so a full drop plan (per-path drop
# points / drop glue) requires the resource checker's finalize-plan
# machinery, which a SemanticDelta does not carry — the exact prerequisite
# for richer rows. Every other ownership row is typed-empty here, never
# invented.
def proof_drop_plan_rows(delta: SemanticDelta) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for row in delta.ownership_delta do
    if proof_own_word_has_sink(&row.before) || proof_own_word_has_sink(&row.after) then
      out.push(proof_drop_plan_row_text(&row))
    end
  end
  out
end

# Whether a §11 dirty word newly carries the alloc class (bit 1 — the §11
# payload marks allocation as the word's low bit; the same bit §36 check 8
# counts).
def proof_word_has_alloc(word: Int) -> Bool
  (word / 1) % 2 == 1
end

# The allocation evidence delta of ONE delta + ONE budget (derivation step
# 9): the "<fn-key> alloc <before-bits> -> <after-bits>" rows of the effect
# delta rows whose after view newly carries the alloc class (bit 1), in the
# delta's own row order, plus the budget's RESERVED allocation byte cap.
# used_bytes stays None (the exact prerequisite is documented on
# AllocationDelta: the §11 view carries no allocation byte count).
def proof_allocation_delta(budget: ChangeBudget, delta: SemanticDelta) -> AllocationDelta
  var rows: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for row in delta.effect_delta do
    if proof_word_has_alloc(row.after.bits) && !proof_word_has_alloc(row.before.bits) then
      rows.push(row.function.clone() + " alloc " + row.before.bits.to_string() + " -> " +
        row.after.bits.to_string())
    end
  end
  AllocationDelta {
    rows: rows,
    budget_bytes: budget.allocation_budget_bytes,
    used_bytes: Option::None
  }
end

# The evidence mapping of ONE stage group (see CLAIM DISCIPLINE): the
# access / resource / MIR stages are exposed SEPARATELY under P0-16 and
# each maps through proof_evidence_status (true -> Verified; false ->
# Failed when captured, Unavailable otherwise).

# (fourth-audit P0-16) The budget status of a verdict list: an empty list
# is the only Verified verdict; any violation is Failed. Unavailable is
# reserved for an assembly with no complete delta to check.
def proof_budget_status(violations: Vec[String]) -> VerificationStatus
  if violations.len() == 0 then
    VerificationStatus::Verified
  else
    VerificationStatus::Failed
  end
end

# (fourth-audit P0-16) The affected-tests COMPLETENESS status: the caller
# supplied the test rows (Verified), or the delta has nothing to enumerate
# (Verified); affected entities with no test rows supplied is Unavailable
# (never Failed and never complete).
def proof_affected_tests_status(bundle: PatchEvidenceBundle, delta: SemanticDelta) -> VerificationStatus
  if bundle.affected_tests.len() > 0 then
    VerificationStatus::Verified
  elsif delta.affected.len() == 0 then
    VerificationStatus::Verified
  else
    VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  end
end

# (fourth-audit P0-16) The equivalence status: a PROVEN §41 result is
# Verified, an unproven result (tested / unknown / counterexample) is
# Failed, and no result held is Unavailable.
def proof_equivalence_status(equivalence: Option[EquivalenceResult]) -> VerificationStatus
  match equivalence
  when Option::None then
    VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  when Option::Some(r) then
    if equivalence_result_is_proven(r) then
      VerificationStatus::Verified
    else
      VerificationStatus::Failed
    end
  end
end

# (fourth-audit P0-16) The SPAN combination of two sides' statuses: a
# stage property is Verified only when BOTH sides verified it; either side
# unavailable makes it Unavailable; otherwise it failed somewhere.
def proof_span_status(a: VerificationStatus, b: VerificationStatus) -> VerificationStatus
  match a
  when VerificationStatus::Verified then b
  when VerificationStatus::Failed then
    match b
    when VerificationStatus::Unavailable then VerificationStatus::Unavailable
    when _ then VerificationStatus::Failed
    end
  when VerificationStatus::Unavailable then VerificationStatus::Unavailable
  end
end

# Applies ONE evidence bundle to an assembled patch (third audit item 29):
# the caller-supplied surfaces are copied onto the patch verbatim — the
# source delta, the obligation rows, the extra allocation rows (appended
# AFTER the delta-derived alloc-class rows), the affected tests, the
# coverage / performance rows and the §41 equivalence result. A None source
# delta leaves the defaulted empty SourceDelta; a None equivalence leaves
# the gate unproven (the budget gate reports the missing result when the
# budget declares an equivalence requirement). The bundle is NEVER turned
# into a claim: it is evidence the caller holds.
def proof_patch_with_evidence(
  patch: ProofCarryingPatch,
  bundle: PatchEvidenceBundle
) -> ProofCarryingPatch
  var out = patch
  match bundle.source_delta
  when Option::Some(sd) then out.source_delta = sd
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  # (audit item 9) the affected closure's shared completeness rides the
  # patch's analysis rows (the ONE attachment point every assembler uses —
  # proof_patch_of_delta / proof_patch_between / proof_patch_of_status all
  # end in this function).
  match bundle.affected
  when Option::Some(affected) then
    out.analysis_completeness = Vec::from([completeness_info_render(affected.completeness_info.clone())])
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  out.obligation_results = bundle.obligation_results
  out.affected_tests = bundle.affected_tests
  out.coverage_delta = bundle.coverage_delta_rows
  out.performance_delta = bundle.performance_delta_rows
  out.equivalence = bundle.equivalence
  var alloc = out.allocation_delta
  for row in bundle.allocation_delta_rows do
    alloc.rows.push(row.clone())
  end
  out.allocation_delta = alloc
  out
end

# Assembles ONE report over ONE §31 delta + ONE budget + ONE evidence
# record + an optional item-29 evidence bundle: derives the report's flat
# lists and item-29 evidence rows from the delta (the module doc's steps
# 1-5 + 8-9), runs the §36 envelope AND the equivalence gate (step 6) and
# sets the typed stage statuses from the evidence (step 7 — the evidence
# mapping above; fourth-audit P0-16). Nothing a delta alone carries can
# prove that a pipeline stage ran; the evidence record is the only source
# for the stages it captured, and an uncaptured stage is Unavailable.
pub def proof_patch_of_delta(
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  delta: SemanticDelta,
  evidence: VerifiedCompilationEvidence,
  bundle: PatchEvidenceBundle = PatchEvidenceBundle {}
) -> ProofCarryingPatch
  let rows = proof_patch_rows_of(&budget, &delta, &bundle.equivalence)
  let patch = ProofCarryingPatch {
    semantic_delta: delta,
    parse_status: proof_evidence_status(&evidence, "parse".to_string(), evidence.parse_ok),
    resolve_status: proof_evidence_status(&evidence, "resolve".to_string(), evidence.resolution_ok),
    type_status: proof_evidence_status(&evidence, "type".to_string(), evidence.type_ok),
    access_status: proof_evidence_status(&evidence, "access".to_string(), evidence.access_ok),
    resource_status: proof_evidence_status(&evidence, "resource".to_string(), evidence.resource_ok),
    mir_status: proof_evidence_status(&evidence, "mir".to_string(), evidence.mir_verify_ok),
    post_mono_mir_status: proof_evidence_status(&evidence, "post-mono-mir".to_string(),
      evidence.mono_verify_ok),
    post_opt_mir_status: proof_evidence_status(&evidence, "post-opt-mir".to_string(),
      evidence.post_opt_mir_verify_ok),
    effects_status: proof_evidence_status(&evidence, "effects".to_string(), evidence.effect_verify_ok),
    capabilities_status: proof_evidence_status(&evidence, "capabilities".to_string(),
      evidence.capability_contract_ok),
    abi_status: proof_evidence_status(&evidence, "abi".to_string(), evidence.abi_verify_ok),
    budget_status: proof_budget_status(rows.budget_result.clone()),
    affected_tests_status: proof_affected_tests_status(&bundle, &delta),
    equivalence_status: proof_equivalence_status(bundle.equivalence.clone()),
    contract_delta: rows.contract_delta.clone(),
    effect_delta: rows.effect_delta.clone(),
    capability_delta: rows.capability_delta.clone(),
    unsafe_delta: rows.unsafe_delta.clone(),
    abi_delta: rows.abi_delta.clone(),
    public_api_delta: rows.public_api_delta.clone(),
    drop_plan_delta: rows.drop_plan_delta.clone(),
    allocation_delta: rows.allocation_delta.clone(),
    budget_result: rows.budget_result.clone()
  }
  proof_patch_with_evidence(patch, bundle)
end

# (fourth-audit P0-18) The STATUS assembly: a Complete delta assembles
# exactly like proof_patch_of_delta; an Unavailable delta REFUSES — the
# patch carries the missing-delta reason, a "budget:delta-unavailable"
# refusal row, budget_status Unavailable and affected-tests Unavailable.
# No caller can turn a missing old snapshot into an empty delta plus a
# passing budget through this path.
pub def proof_patch_of_status(
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  status: DeltaStatus,
  evidence: VerifiedCompilationEvidence,
  bundle: PatchEvidenceBundle = PatchEvidenceBundle {}
) -> ProofCarryingPatch
  match status
  when DeltaStatus::Complete(d) then
    proof_patch_of_delta(&budget, &d, &evidence, bundle)
  when DeltaStatus::Unavailable(reason) then
    let empty = semantic_delta_empty()
    var patch = proof_patch_of_delta(&budget, &empty, &evidence, bundle)
    patch.delta_unavailable = Option::Some(reason.clone())
    patch.budget_result = Vec::from(["budget:delta-unavailable " + reason.clone()])
    patch.budget_status = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
    patch.affected_tests_status = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
    patch
  end
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# THE VERIFICATION-LEVEL GATE (audit order P0-15)
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# ONE transaction's claimable verification level, ordered weakest ->
# strongest. A verified proof patch is emitted ONLY at VerifiedFull — the
# level at which the FULL pipeline ran (final MIR included) and the
# authoritative snapshot delta exists. The two weaker levels are the
# honest partial claims: ProvisionalFrontEnd = the transaction stopped
# before final MIR/snapshot creation; VerifiedFrontend = the front-end
# chain (parse -> resolve -> type -> access -> resource) verified but the
# authoritative snapshot stage was unavailable. Neither can ever produce a
# VerifiedProofPatch: verified_proof_patch structurally refuses them, and
# proof_patch_of_level assembles a refusal patch (budget_status and
# affected-tests Unavailable, the level word in the refusal row) for every
# weaker level instead of a reportable patch.
pub enum VerificationLevel
  ProvisionalFrontEnd
  VerifiedFrontend
  VerifiedFull
end

# The canonical level word (the wire / render vocabulary).
pub def verification_level_word(level: VerificationLevel) -> String
  match level
  when VerificationLevel::ProvisionalFrontEnd then "provisional-front-end"
  when VerificationLevel::VerifiedFrontend then "verified-frontend"
  when VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull then "verified-full"
  end
end

# The level of a canonical word (Option::None outside the three).
pub def verification_level_of_word(word: String) -> Option[VerificationLevel]
  if word == "provisional-front-end" then
    return Option::Some(VerificationLevel::ProvisionalFrontEnd)
  end
  if word == "verified-frontend" then
    return Option::Some(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFrontend)
  end
  if word == "verified-full" then
    return Option::Some(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull)
  end
  Option::None
end

# The ladder rank (0 / 1 / 2) a policy minimum compares against.
pub def verification_level_rank(level: VerificationLevel) -> Int
  match level
  when VerificationLevel::ProvisionalFrontEnd then 0
  when VerificationLevel::VerifiedFrontend then 1
  when VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull then 2
  end
end

# ONE proof-gated patch: the ProofCarryingPatch a VerifiedFull transaction
# assembled plus the transaction's final proof hash (the digest over the
# transaction's canonical render — semantic_server.tg's
# verified_edit_transaction_render). This is the FULLY VERIFIED class
# (the audit's "fully verified" claim): its ONE sanctioned construction is
# verified_proof_patch below, and that constructor requires ALL THREE
# structural preconditions IN THE CONSTRUCTOR — level == VerifiedFull,
# proof_patch_all_verified(patch) (every one of the fourteen stage
# statuses Verified — never merely not-failed, never Unavailable) and an
# AVAILABLE delta. No caller can obtain the value from a partial patch.
# Callers holding a weaker-but-honest claim use the distinct classes below
# (CompilationVerifiedPatch / BudgetVerifiedPatch / TestVerifiedPatch)
# instead of a partial object typed as a verified proof.
pub struct VerifiedProofPatch
  level: VerificationLevel
  patch: ProofCarryingPatch
  proof_hash: StableDigest
end

# The LEVEL-GATED patch assembly: VerifiedFull assembles exactly like
# proof_patch_of_status; every weaker level REFUSES — the returned patch
# carries the "budget:verification-level-unavailable" row, budget_status
# Unavailable and affected-tests Unavailable, so no consumer can read it as
# a verified patch. This is the ONE construction entry the verified-edit
# transaction uses (semantic_server.tg's session_apply_verified_edit).
pub def proof_patch_of_level(
  level: VerificationLevel,
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  status: DeltaStatus,
  evidence: VerifiedCompilationEvidence,
  bundle: PatchEvidenceBundle = PatchEvidenceBundle {}
) -> ProofCarryingPatch
  match level
  when VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull then
    proof_patch_of_status(&budget, status, &evidence, bundle)
  when _ then
    let reason = "verification level " + verification_level_word(level) +
      ": a proof patch requires " + verification_level_word(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull) +
      " (the transaction stopped before final MIR/snapshot creation)"
    var patch = proof_patch_of_status(&budget,
      DeltaStatus::Unavailable(reason.clone()), &evidence, bundle)
    patch.budget_result = Vec::from([
      "budget:verification-level-unavailable " + reason
    ])
    patch.budget_status = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
    patch.affected_tests_status = VerificationStatus::Unavailable
    patch
  end
end

# The structural gate: Some(VerifiedProofPatch) ONLY for a VerifiedFull
# level whose patch is FULLY verified — every one of the fourteen stage
# statuses Verified (proof_patch_all_verified: not merely budget status,
# and never a Failed/Unavailable stage) — with an AVAILABLE delta (no
# delta_unavailable reason). Every weaker level, every partial patch and
# every unavailable delta is None: a ProvisionalFrontEnd /
# VerifiedFrontend transaction, or a VerifiedFull transaction missing any
# compiler stage (e.g. the post-mono checkpoint), is structurally
# incapable of serializing as a verified proof patch.
pub def verified_proof_patch(
  level: VerificationLevel, patch: ProofCarryingPatch, proof_hash: StableDigest
) -> Option[VerifiedProofPatch]
  if level == VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull &&
     proof_patch_all_verified(&patch) &&
     patch.delta_unavailable.is_none() then
    Option::Some(VerifiedProofPatch {
      level: level,
      patch: patch,
      proof_hash: proof_hash
    })
  else
    Option::None
  end
end

# The canonical spelling of the fully verified constructor (the same
# structural gate as verified_proof_patch — the class the task vocabulary
# calls FullyVerifiedPatch). Kept as ONE function so no construction path
# can drift.
pub def fully_verified_patch(
  level: VerificationLevel, patch: ProofCarryingPatch, proof_hash: StableDigest
) -> Option[VerifiedProofPatch]
  verified_proof_patch(level, patch, proof_hash)
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# THE SPAN ASSEMBLY — ONE ProofCarryingPatch between two compilations
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# proof_patch_between assembles the CHANGE patch over the OLD and NEW
# evidence records of the two compilations a change spans. The stage
# flags are the evidence mapping ANDed across BOTH records: parses :=
# old.parse_ok && new.parse_ok, resolves := old.resolution_ok &&
# new.resolution_ok, types := old.type_ok && new.type_ok, ownership :=
# the ownership group of the old side AND the ownership group of the new
# side. A stage property is claimed only when BOTH compilations the patch
# spans established it — one unverified endpoint leaves the property
# unproven for the span (claim discipline). old_delta, when supplied, is
# the §31 diff the caller computed between the two compilations'
# finalized states (semantic_delta_of over the sessions' snapshots — the
# delta computed from real evidence); the report rows + budget verdict
# derive from it (the module doc's steps 1-6 + 8-9). When it is NOT
# supplied
# the report's delta stays the empty delta (which verifies against ANY
# budget), the flags still come from the evidence, and the caller fills
# the real delta by re-running proof_patch_of_delta with it — the
# between-form never fabricates a delta. The optional item-29 evidence
# bundle rides exactly as in proof_patch_of_delta (defaulted empty).
pub def proof_patch_between(
  old: VerifiedCompilationEvidence,
  new: VerifiedCompilationEvidence,
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  old_delta: Option[SemanticDelta],
  bundle: PatchEvidenceBundle = PatchEvidenceBundle {}
) -> ProofCarryingPatch
  match old_delta
  when Option::Some(d) then
    let rows = proof_patch_rows_of(&budget, &d, &bundle.equivalence)
    let patch = ProofCarryingPatch {
      semantic_delta: d,
      parse_status: proof_span_status(
        proof_evidence_status(&old, "parse".to_string(), old.parse_ok),
        proof_evidence_status(&new, "parse".to_string(), new.parse_ok)),
      resolve_status: proof_span_status(
        proof_evidence_status(&old, "resolve".to_string(), old.resolution_ok),
        proof_evidence_status(&new, "resolve".to_string(), new.resolution_ok)),
      type_status: proof_span_status(
        proof_evidence_status(&old, "type".to_string(), old.type_ok),
        proof_evidence_status(&new, "type".to_string(), new.type_ok)),
      access_status: proof_span_status(
        proof_evidence_status(&old, "access".to_string(), old.access_ok),
        proof_evidence_status(&new, "access".to_string(), new.access_ok)),
      resource_status: proof_span_status(
        proof_evidence_status(&old, "resource".to_string(), old.resource_ok),
        proof_evidence_status(&new, "resource".to_string(), new.resource_ok)),
      mir_status: proof_span_status(
        proof_evidence_status(&old, "mir".to_string(), old.mir_verify_ok),
        proof_evidence_status(&new, "mir".to_string(), new.mir_verify_ok)),
      post_mono_mir_status: proof_span_status(
        proof_evidence_status(&old, "post-mono-mir".to_string(), old.mono_verify_ok),
        proof_evidence_status(&new, "post-mono-mir".to_string(), new.mono_verify_ok)),
      post_opt_mir_status: proof_span_status(
        proof_evidence_status(&old, "post-opt-mir".to_string(), old.post_opt_mir_verify_ok),
        proof_evidence_status(&new, "post-opt-mir".to_string(), new.post_opt_mir_verify_ok)),
      effects_status: proof_span_status(
        proof_evidence_status(&old, "effects".to_string(), old.effect_verify_ok),
        proof_evidence_status(&new, "effects".to_string(), new.effect_verify_ok)),
      capabilities_status: proof_span_status(
        proof_evidence_status(&old, "capabilities".to_string(), old.capability_contract_ok),
        proof_evidence_status(&new, "capabilities".to_string(), new.capability_contract_ok)),
      abi_status: proof_span_status(
        proof_evidence_status(&old, "abi".to_string(), old.abi_verify_ok),
        proof_evidence_status(&new, "abi".to_string(), new.abi_verify_ok)),
      budget_status: proof_budget_status(rows.budget_result.clone()),
      affected_tests_status: proof_affected_tests_status(&bundle, &d),
      equivalence_status: proof_equivalence_status(bundle.equivalence.clone()),
      contract_delta: rows.contract_delta.clone(),
      effect_delta: rows.effect_delta.clone(),
      capability_delta: rows.capability_delta.clone(),
      unsafe_delta: rows.unsafe_delta.clone(),
      abi_delta: rows.abi_delta.clone(),
      public_api_delta: rows.public_api_delta.clone(),
      drop_plan_delta: rows.drop_plan_delta.clone(),
      allocation_delta: rows.allocation_delta.clone(),
      budget_result: rows.budget_result.clone()
    }
    proof_patch_with_evidence(patch, bundle)
  when Option::None then
    # (fourth-audit P0-18) a missing old delta is UNAVAILABLE — never an
    # empty delta plus a passing budget. The refusal patch carries the
    # reason and budget_status Unavailable.
    proof_patch_of_status(&budget,
      DeltaStatus::Unavailable("missing old semantic delta: the change delta cannot be computed".to_string()),
      &new, bundle)
  end
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The §36-rule unsafe-marker rows
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The rows of change_budget.tg's EXACT COUNTING RULE (check 7 — audit item
# 16): the CREATED UnsafeFact rows of the delta's unsafe_delta, rendered in
# the marker vocabulary (semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text) in the delta's
# own (sorted) row order. The ownership/effect-row sources of the former
# rule never participate.
def proof_unsafe_rows(delta: SemanticDelta) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for fact in delta.unsafe_delta.created do
    out.push(semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text(&fact))
  end
  out
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The claim surface — the typed status renderers (fourth-audit P0-16)
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The stages, in the fixed order the renderers use:
# parse / resolve / type / access / resource / mir-after-lowering /
# post-mono mir / post-opt mir / effects / capabilities-contracts / abi /
# budget / affected-tests completeness / equivalence.

# (fourth-audit P0-16) THE all-verified predicate: every one of the
# fourteen statuses is Verified — NOT merely not-failed. A patch whose
# post-opt MIR or ABI status is Unavailable (the driver route captures
# neither) answers false here; complete verification is never reported
# from absent evidence.
pub def proof_patch_all_verified(patch: ProofCarryingPatch) -> Bool
  verification_status_is_verified(patch.parse_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.resolve_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.type_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.access_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.resource_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.mir_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.post_mono_mir_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.post_opt_mir_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.effects_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.capabilities_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.abi_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.budget_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.affected_tests_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.equivalence_status)
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# THE TRUTHFUL PATCH-CLAIM CLASSES (P0 proof-gating)
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The claim ladder below the fully verified class. A consumer that holds
# only PART of the fourteen-status evidence must name the truthful class,
# never a partial object typed VerifiedProofPatch:
#
#   CompilationVerifiedPatch — the ELEVEN COMPILER stages are Verified
#     (parse / resolve / type / access / resource / mir-after-lowering /
#     post-mono mir / post-opt mir / effects / capabilities-contracts /
#     abi) at VerifiedFull with an available delta. The compiler pipeline
#     verified the change; the budget / affected-tests / equivalence
#     surfaces may still be Unavailable or Failed.
#   BudgetVerifiedPatch — the compilation claim plus budget_status
#     Verified over a complete delta with an EMPTY violation list (the §36
#     envelope accepted the change).
#   TestVerifiedPatch — the compilation claim plus the affected-tests
#     completeness status Verified and the §41 equivalence status Verified
#     (a PROVEN equivalence result). Tests are evidence, not proof: this
#     class never implies the other stages.
#   VerifiedProofPatch — the FULL fourteen-status class
#     (proof_patch_all_verified), i.e. the task vocabulary's
#     FullyVerifiedPatch.
#
# Every constructor returns Option and carries its predicate INLINE so no
# construction path can drift from its claim.

# The ELEVEN compiler verification stages of a patch: every one Verified.
pub def proof_patch_compiler_verified(patch: ProofCarryingPatch) -> Bool
  verification_status_is_verified(patch.parse_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.resolve_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.type_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.access_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.resource_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.mir_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.post_mono_mir_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.post_opt_mir_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.effects_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.capabilities_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.abi_status)
end

# The §36 envelope claim: the compiler stages plus a Verified budget
# status over an empty violation list.
pub def proof_patch_budget_verified(patch: ProofCarryingPatch) -> Bool
  proof_patch_compiler_verified(&patch) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.budget_status) &&
    patch.budget_result.len() == 0
end

# The test/equivalence claim: the compiler stages plus Verified
# affected-tests completeness and a PROVEN §41 equivalence result.
pub def proof_patch_test_verified(patch: ProofCarryingPatch) -> Bool
  proof_patch_compiler_verified(&patch) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.affected_tests_status) &&
    verification_status_is_verified(patch.equivalence_status)
end

# The strongest truthful class word of a patch's fourteen statuses
# ("fully-verified" / "test-verified" / "budget-verified" /
# "compilation-verified" / "unverified"). The word is a CLAIM over the
# patch's own evidence — never a level claim (the level participates only
# in the class constructors below).
pub def proof_patch_verified_class_word(patch: ProofCarryingPatch) -> String
  if proof_patch_all_verified(&patch) then
    "fully-verified"
  elsif proof_patch_test_verified(&patch) then
    "test-verified"
  elsif proof_patch_budget_verified(&patch) then
    "budget-verified"
  elsif proof_patch_compiler_verified(&patch) then
    "compilation-verified"
  else
    "unverified"
  end
end

# ONE compilation-verified patch: the ELEVEN compiler stages Verified at
# VerifiedFull with an available delta.
pub struct CompilationVerifiedPatch
  level: VerificationLevel
  patch: ProofCarryingPatch
  proof_hash: StableDigest
end

# ONE budget-verified patch: the compilation claim plus the Verified §36
# envelope verdict.
pub struct BudgetVerifiedPatch
  level: VerificationLevel
  patch: ProofCarryingPatch
  proof_hash: StableDigest
end

# ONE test-verified patch: the compilation claim plus Verified
# affected-tests completeness and a PROVEN equivalence result.
pub struct TestVerifiedPatch
  level: VerificationLevel
  patch: ProofCarryingPatch
  proof_hash: StableDigest
end

pub def compilation_verified_patch(
  level: VerificationLevel, patch: ProofCarryingPatch, proof_hash: StableDigest
) -> Option[CompilationVerifiedPatch]
  if level == VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull &&
     proof_patch_compiler_verified(&patch) &&
     patch.delta_unavailable.is_none() then
    Option::Some(CompilationVerifiedPatch {
      level: level,
      patch: patch,
      proof_hash: proof_hash
    })
  else
    Option::None
  end
end

pub def budget_verified_patch(
  level: VerificationLevel, patch: ProofCarryingPatch, proof_hash: StableDigest
) -> Option[BudgetVerifiedPatch]
  if level == VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull &&
     proof_patch_budget_verified(&patch) &&
     patch.delta_unavailable.is_none() then
    Option::Some(BudgetVerifiedPatch {
      level: level,
      patch: patch,
      proof_hash: proof_hash
    })
  else
    Option::None
  end
end

pub def test_verified_patch(
  level: VerificationLevel, patch: ProofCarryingPatch, proof_hash: StableDigest
) -> Option[TestVerifiedPatch]
  if level == VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull &&
     proof_patch_test_verified(&patch) &&
     patch.delta_unavailable.is_none() then
    Option::Some(TestVerifiedPatch {
      level: level,
      patch: patch,
      proof_hash: proof_hash
    })
  else
    Option::None
  end
end

# Every stage rendered as "<stage>: <status word>" in fixed order — the
# full verification surface (Verified / Failed / Unavailable per stage).
pub def proof_patch_verification_rows(patch: ProofCarryingPatch) -> Vec[String]
  Vec::from([
    "parse: " + verification_status_word(patch.parse_status),
    "resolve: " + verification_status_word(patch.resolve_status),
    "type: " + verification_status_word(patch.type_status),
    "access: " + verification_status_word(patch.access_status),
    "resource: " + verification_status_word(patch.resource_status),
    "mir-after-lowering: " + verification_status_word(patch.mir_status),
    "post-mono-mir: " + verification_status_word(patch.post_mono_mir_status),
    "post-opt-mir: " + verification_status_word(patch.post_opt_mir_status),
    "effects: " + verification_status_word(patch.effects_status),
    "capabilities-contracts: " + verification_status_word(patch.capabilities_status),
    "abi: " + verification_status_word(patch.abi_status),
    "budget: " + verification_status_word(patch.budget_status),
    "affected-tests: " + verification_status_word(patch.affected_tests_status),
    "equivalence: " + verification_status_word(patch.equivalence_status)
  ])
end

# The proven-field name list: the stages whose status is Verified, in the
# fixed pipeline order, rendered with the status word ("parse: verified").
# An empty list means no stage property is claimed — the fail-closed claim
# surface, never a denial of a property the pipeline actually established.
pub def proof_patch_proven_fields(patch: ProofCarryingPatch) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for row in proof_patch_verification_rows(patch) do
    if row.ends_with(": verified") then
      out.push(row)
    end
  end
  out
end

# (fourth-audit P0-18) The patch's delta status: Unavailable when the
# delta_unavailable reason was recorded, else Complete over the carried
# delta.
pub def proof_patch_delta_status(patch: ProofCarryingPatch) -> DeltaStatus
  match patch.delta_unavailable
  when Option::Some(reason) then
    DeltaStatus::Unavailable(reason)
  when Option::None then
    DeltaStatus::Complete(patch.semantic_delta.clone())
  end
end

# The delta-unavailable reason text ("" when the delta is complete).
pub def proof_patch_delta_unavailable_reason(patch: ProofCarryingPatch) -> String
  match patch.delta_unavailable
  when Option::Some(reason) then reason
  when Option::None then "".to_string()
  end
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The third-audit item-29 lane (unit-style rows)
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The sibling style of change_budget.tg's budget_lane_check: the rows are
# self-checking helpers the test-file lane (tests/proof_patch_test.tg)
# calls. Each row assembles a minimal patch fixture (the delta records ARE
# the assembler's input — no snapshot is needed) and asserts the item-29
# evidence surfaces and the item-32 equivalence gate:
#   P1 the claim-nothing patch: every new evidence surface is defaulted
#      empty (empty SourceDelta, no drop-plan / obligation / coverage /
#      performance rows, an empty AllocationDelta with no byte totals, no
#      equivalence result).
#   P2 the delta-derived surfaces: the alloc-class effect row (bit 1) fills
#      allocation_delta.rows, and the sink-bearing ownership row fills
#      drop_plan_delta (the let/inout row emits nothing).
#   P3 the bundle surfaces: a full PatchEvidenceBundle is carried onto the
#      patch verbatim (source delta, obligations, affected tests, coverage
#      / performance rows, the equivalence result), and the caller
#      allocation rows append after the derived row.
#   P4 the item-32 gate through the assembler: the refactor budget with no
#      equivalence result carries the "budget:equivalence-required" row;
#      a proven result clears it.
#   P5/P6 a tested result clears the gate only when the budget does not
#      demand a proof (require_proven = false) — under the default
#      refactor requirement it violates (tests are evidence, not proof).
#   P12 the truthful class ladder (P0 proof-gating): only the all-fourteen
#      Verified patch constructs VerifiedProofPatch / fully_verified_patch
#      (a Failed/Unavailable stage or an unavailable delta refuses every
#      class); the weaker classes name their own predicates
#      (compilation / budget / test) and
#      proof_patch_verified_class_word reports the strongest truthful
#      class of a patch's statuses.

def proof_lane_expect(inout out: Vec[String], name: String, cond: Bool) -> Unit
  if !cond then
    out.push(name + ": expectation failed")
  end
  ()
end

def proof_lane_has_row_prefix(rows: Vec[String], prefix: String) -> Bool
  for r in rows do
    if r.starts_with(prefix) then
      return true
    end
  end
  false
end

def proof_lane_evidence() -> VerifiedCompilationEvidence
  verified_compilation_evidence("rev-1".to_string(), true, true, true, true, true,
    true, true, true, true, true, true)
end

# One delta carrying one newly-alloc-class effect row (before bits 0 ->
# after bits 1 — the §11 alloc bit).
def proof_lane_alloc_delta() -> SemanticDelta
  var delta = semantic_delta_empty()
  var rows: Vec[EffectDelta] = Vec::new()
  rows.push(EffectDelta {
    function: "m::f".to_string(),
    before: EffectSummaryView { bits: 0, capabilities: Vec::new() },
    after: EffectSummaryView { bits: 1, capabilities: Vec::new() }
  })
  delta.effect_delta = rows
  delta
end

# One delta carrying two ownership rows: a sink-bearing transition (the
# drop-relevant one) and a let -> inout transition (no drop plan).
def proof_lane_ownership_delta() -> SemanticDelta
  var delta = semantic_delta_empty()
  var rows: Vec[OwnershipDelta] = Vec::new()
  rows.push(OwnershipDelta {
    function: "m::f".to_string(),
    place: "x".to_string(),
    before: "let".to_string(),
    after: "let;sink".to_string()
  })
  rows.push(OwnershipDelta {
    function: "m::g".to_string(),
    place: "y".to_string(),
    before: "let".to_string(),
    after: "inout".to_string()
  })
  delta.ownership_delta = rows
  delta
end

pub def proof_patch_lane_check() -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()

  # P1 — the claim-nothing patch: every new evidence surface is defaulted.
  let empty = proof_patch_new()
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P1-source-delta-defaulted-empty",
    empty.source_delta.changed_files.len() == 0 && empty.source_delta.hunk_hashes.len() == 0)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P1-drop-plan-defaulted-empty", empty.drop_plan_delta.len() == 0)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P1-obligation-results-defaulted-empty",
    empty.obligation_results.len() == 0)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P1-allocation-delta-defaulted-empty",
    empty.allocation_delta.rows.len() == 0 &&
    empty.allocation_delta.budget_bytes.is_none() &&
    empty.allocation_delta.used_bytes.is_none())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P1-coverage-performance-defaulted-empty",
    empty.coverage_delta.len() == 0 && empty.performance_delta.len() == 0)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P1-equivalence-defaulted-none", empty.equivalence.is_none())

  # P2 — the delta-derived surfaces.
  let derived_alloc = proof_patch_of_delta(&ChangeBudget {}, &proof_lane_alloc_delta(),
    &proof_lane_evidence())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P2-allocation-row-derived",
    derived_alloc.allocation_delta.rows.len() == 1 &&
    derived_alloc.allocation_delta.rows[0] == "m::f alloc 0 -> 1" &&
    derived_alloc.allocation_delta.budget_bytes.is_none() &&
    derived_alloc.allocation_delta.used_bytes.is_none())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P2-allocation-row-drop-not-derived",
    derived_alloc.drop_plan_delta.len() == 0)
  # (fourth-audit P0-17) the drop_plan_delta IS the §31 typed diff: a delta
  # carrying one DropPlanDelta row hands it to the patch whole (the
  # ownership-convention reconstruction is gone).
  var drop_delta = semantic_delta_empty()
  var drop_rows: Vec[DropPlanDelta] = Vec::new()
  drop_rows.push(DropPlanDelta {
    function: "m::f".to_string(),
    place: "x".to_string(),
    before: Vec::from([DropSiteDelta {
      drop_site: "m::f|normal|B1".to_string(),
      conditional_paths: Vec::new(),
      kind: "scope-exit".to_string()
    }]),
    after: Vec::from([DropSiteDelta {
      drop_site: "m::f|false|B3".to_string(),
      conditional_paths: Vec::from(["branch:false".to_string()]),
      kind: "branch-cleanup".to_string()
    }])
  })
  drop_delta.drop_plan_delta = drop_rows
  let derived_drop = proof_patch_of_delta(&ChangeBudget {}, &drop_delta, &proof_lane_evidence())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P2-drop-plan-typed-row-carried",
    derived_drop.drop_plan_delta.len() == 1 &&
    derived_drop.drop_plan_delta[0].function == "m::f" &&
    derived_drop.drop_plan_delta[0].place == "x" &&
    derived_drop.drop_plan_delta[0].after.len() == 1 &&
    derived_drop.drop_plan_delta[0].after[0].kind == "branch-cleanup" &&
    derived_drop.drop_plan_delta[0].after[0].conditional_paths[0] == "branch:false")
  # The old sink-row reconstruction no longer drives the field: an
  # ownership-only delta leaves drop_plan_delta empty (the typed diff is
  # the resource checker's persisted plan, not a convention scan).
  let derived_own = proof_patch_of_delta(&ChangeBudget {}, &proof_lane_ownership_delta(),
    &proof_lane_evidence())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P2-drop-plan-not-reconstructed-from-ownership",
    derived_own.drop_plan_delta.len() == 0)

  # P3 — the bundle surfaces carried onto the patch.
  let bundle = PatchEvidenceBundle {
    source_delta: Option::Some(SourceDelta {
      changed_files: Vec::from(["src/a.tg".to_string()]),
      hunk_hashes: Vec::from(["h1".to_string(), "h2".to_string()])
    }),
    obligation_results: Vec::from(["m::f Clone bound: satisfied".to_string()]),
    allocation_delta_rows: Vec::from(["m::f measured 128 bytes".to_string()]),
    affected_tests: Vec::from(["test_f".to_string()]),
    coverage_delta_rows: Vec::from(["m::f +3 covered lines".to_string()]),
    performance_delta_rows: Vec::from(["m::f 120ns -> 100ns".to_string()]),
    equivalence: Option::Some(equivalence_proven_finite("symbolic-finite"))
  }
  let carried = proof_patch_of_delta(&budget_refactor_default(), &proof_lane_alloc_delta(),
    &proof_lane_evidence(), bundle)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P3-source-delta-carried",
    carried.source_delta.changed_files.len() == 1 &&
    carried.source_delta.changed_files[0] == "src/a.tg" &&
    carried.source_delta.hunk_hashes.len() == 2)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P3-obligation-results-carried",
    carried.obligation_results.len() == 1)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P3-affected-tests-carried", carried.affected_tests.len() == 1)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P3-coverage-and-performance-carried",
    carried.coverage_delta.len() == 1 && carried.performance_delta.len() == 1)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P3-equivalence-carried", carried.equivalence.is_some())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P3-allocation-rows-appended",
    carried.allocation_delta.rows.len() == 2 &&
    carried.allocation_delta.rows[1] == "m::f measured 128 bytes")
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P3-equivalence-requirement-satisfied",
    !proof_lane_has_row_prefix(carried.budget_result.clone(), "budget:equivalence-required"))

  # P4 — the gate through the assembler: no result under the refactor
  # budget violates; a proven result clears it.
  let missing = proof_patch_of_delta(&budget_refactor_default(), &semantic_delta_empty(),
    &proof_lane_evidence())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P4-refactor-gate-missing-result-violates",
    proof_lane_has_row_prefix(missing.budget_result.clone(), "budget:equivalence-required"))
  let proven_bundle = PatchEvidenceBundle {
    equivalence: Option::Some(equivalence_structural("normalized-mir"))
  }
  let proven = proof_patch_of_delta(&budget_refactor_default(), &semantic_delta_empty(),
    &proof_lane_evidence(), proven_bundle)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P4-refactor-gate-proven-result-passes",
    !proof_lane_has_row_prefix(proven.budget_result.clone(), "budget:equivalence-required"))

  # P5/P6 — the tested level: evidence, not proof.
  let tested_strict = PatchEvidenceBundle {
    equivalence: Option::Some(equivalence_tested(true, "the differential corpus"))
  }
  let strict = proof_patch_of_delta(&budget_refactor_default(), &semantic_delta_empty(),
    &proof_lane_evidence(), tested_strict)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P5-tested-result-under-proof-demand-violates",
    proof_lane_has_row_prefix(strict.budget_result.clone(), "budget:equivalence-required"))
  let tested_relaxed = PatchEvidenceBundle {
    equivalence: Option::Some(equivalence_tested(true, "the differential corpus"))
  }
  let relaxed = proof_patch_of_delta(
    &budget_refactor_with_level(EquivalenceLevel::StructurallyEquivalent, false),
    &semantic_delta_empty(), &proof_lane_evidence(), tested_relaxed)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P6-tested-result-without-proof-demand-passes",
    !proof_lane_has_row_prefix(relaxed.budget_result.clone(), "budget:equivalence-required"))

  # P7 (fourth-audit P0-16) — the typed verification statuses.
  # The claim-nothing patch: every status Unavailable (never Failed).
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P7-new-patch-statuses-unavailable",
    verification_status_word(empty.post_opt_mir_status) == "unavailable" &&
    verification_status_word(empty.abi_status) == "unavailable" &&
    !proof_patch_all_verified(&empty))
  # (the shared finalized-MIR pipeline) The driver route's captured set
  # now INCLUDES post-mono-mir (the route compiles through
  # finalize_verified_mir, whose unconditional post-mono verify_mir
  # checkpoint the shared entry always runs), so a false mono flag is
  # Failed — never Unavailable — and complete verification is never
  # reported from this capture. Since audit order item 7 the route
  # CAPTURES abi (the real post-lowering verifier), so the false abi flag
  # here is Failed too.
  let route_evidence = verified_compilation_evidence_stages(
    "rev-route".to_string(), true, true, true, true, true, true,
    false,  # mono — a false CAPTURED flag (the checkpoint is a real stage)
    true, true,
    false,  # abi — a false CAPTURED flag (Failed, not Unavailable)
    true,   # capability/contract surface
    verification_stage_names_driver_route())
  let route_patch = proof_patch_of_delta(&ChangeBudget {}, &semantic_delta_empty(), &route_evidence)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P7-route-post-mono-mir-captured-failed",
    verification_status_word(route_patch.post_mono_mir_status) == "failed")
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P7-route-abi-captured-failed",
    verification_status_word(route_patch.abi_status) == "failed")
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P7-route-not-all-verified",
    !proof_patch_all_verified(&route_patch))
  # A false flag for a CAPTURED stage is Failed, not Unavailable.
  let failed_evidence = verified_compilation_evidence("rev-f".to_string(),
    true, false, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true)
  let failed_patch = proof_patch_of_delta(&ChangeBudget {}, &semantic_delta_empty(), &failed_evidence)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P7-captured-false-flag-failed",
    verification_status_word(failed_patch.resolve_status) == "failed")
  # A fully captured, all-true evidence plus a proven equivalence result
  # and an enumerable delta IS all-verified (the positive control).
  let full_bundle = PatchEvidenceBundle {
    equivalence: Option::Some(equivalence_structural("normalized-mir"))
  }
  let full_patch = proof_patch_of_delta(&ChangeBudget {}, &semantic_delta_empty(),
    &proof_lane_evidence(), full_bundle)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P7-all-true-evidence-all-verified",
    proof_patch_all_verified(&full_patch))
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P7-proven-fields-status-words",
    proof_patch_proven_fields(full_patch).len() == 14 &&
    proof_patch_proven_fields(full_patch)[0] == "parse: verified")
  # The status rows render Unavailable words for the claim-nothing patch.
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P7-verification-rows-status-words",
    proof_patch_verification_rows(empty).len() == 14 &&
    proof_patch_verification_rows(empty)[10] == "abi: unavailable")

  # P8 (fourth-audit P0-18) — proof_patch_between with NO old delta is the
  # Unavailable refusal: the refusal row, budget_status Unavailable, the
  # reason recorded, and NEVER a passing budget over the empty delta.
  let between_missing = proof_patch_between(&proof_lane_evidence(), &proof_lane_evidence(),
    &ChangeBudget {}, Option::None)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P8-between-missing-delta-refusal-row",
    proof_lane_has_row_prefix(between_missing.budget_result.clone(), "budget:delta-unavailable"))
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P8-between-missing-delta-budget-unavailable",
    verification_status_word(between_missing.budget_status) == "unavailable")
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P8-between-missing-delta-reason",
    proof_patch_delta_unavailable_reason(between_missing).contains("missing old semantic delta"))
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P8-between-missing-delta-not-all-verified",
    !proof_patch_all_verified(&between_missing))

  # P9 (fourth-audit P0-18) — proof_patch_of_status over an Unavailable
  # status refuses identically; the status helper round-trips.
  let status_patch = proof_patch_of_status(&ChangeBudget {},
    DeltaStatus::Unavailable("missing old snapshot: no baseline".to_string()),
    &proof_lane_evidence())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P9-status-unavailable-refuses",
    verification_status_word(status_patch.budget_status) == "unavailable" &&
    proof_lane_has_row_prefix(status_patch.budget_result.clone(), "budget:delta-unavailable"))
  match proof_patch_delta_status(status_patch)
  when DeltaStatus::Unavailable(reason) then
    proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P9-delta-status-roundtrip",
      reason.contains("missing old snapshot"))
  when DeltaStatus::Complete(_) then
    out.push("P9-delta-status-roundtrip: expected Unavailable, got Complete")
  end

  # P10 (audit order P0-15) — the verification-level gate: only
  # VerifiedFull assembles a reportable patch; ProvisionalFrontEnd /
  # VerifiedFrontend refuse (budget Unavailable, the level refusal row),
  # and the VerifiedProofPatch constructor refuses every weaker level.
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P10-level-words",
    verification_level_word(VerificationLevel::ProvisionalFrontEnd) == "provisional-front-end" &&
    verification_level_word(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFrontend) == "verified-frontend" &&
    verification_level_word(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull) == "verified-full" &&
    verification_level_rank(VerificationLevel::ProvisionalFrontEnd) == 0 &&
    verification_level_rank(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull) == 2)
  match verification_level_of_word("verified-full".to_string())
  when Option::Some(l) then
    proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P10-level-word-roundtrip", verification_level_rank(l) == 2)
  when Option::None then
    out.push("P10-level-word-roundtrip: expected Some, got None")
  end
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P10-unknown-level-word",
    verification_level_of_word("not-a-level".to_string()).is_none())
  let gated_full = proof_patch_of_level(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, &ChangeBudget {},
    DeltaStatus::Complete(semantic_delta_empty()), &proof_lane_evidence())
  let gated_provisional = proof_patch_of_level(VerificationLevel::ProvisionalFrontEnd,
    &ChangeBudget {}, DeltaStatus::Complete(semantic_delta_empty()), &proof_lane_evidence())
  let gated_frontend = proof_patch_of_level(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFrontend,
    &ChangeBudget {}, DeltaStatus::Complete(semantic_delta_empty()), &proof_lane_evidence())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P10-full-level-patch-verifies",
    verification_status_word(gated_full.budget_status) == "verified")
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P10-provisional-level-refuses",
    verification_status_word(gated_provisional.budget_status) == "unavailable" &&
    verification_status_word(gated_provisional.affected_tests_status) == "unavailable" &&
    proof_lane_has_row_prefix(gated_provisional.budget_result.clone(),
      "budget:verification-level-unavailable"))
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P10-frontend-level-refuses",
    verification_status_word(gated_frontend.budget_status) == "unavailable" &&
    proof_lane_has_row_prefix(gated_frontend.budget_result.clone(),
      "budget:verification-level-unavailable"))
  let lane_hash = stable_digest_of("lane-proof-hash".to_string())
  # (P0 proof-gating) The wrapper is the FULLY verified class: the
  # bundle-less gated_full patch carries an Unavailable equivalence
  # status, so its construction is refused (the pre-fix constructor
  # accepted it on the budget status alone). The positive control is the
  # all-fourteen Verified full_patch from P7.
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P10-verified-proof-partial-none",
    verified_proof_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, gated_full.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P10-verified-proof-full-some",
    verified_proof_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, full_patch.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_some())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P10-verified-proof-provisional-none",
    verified_proof_patch(VerificationLevel::ProvisionalFrontEnd, full_patch.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P10-verified-proof-frontend-none",
    verified_proof_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFrontend, full_patch.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none())

  # P11 (audit item 9) — the analysis-completeness attachment: a patch
  # assembled from a bundle carrying an AffectedResult renders the shared
  # completeness record as its ONE analysis row; a bundle without one
  # leaves the rows empty (never an invented claim).
  var affected_lane = AffectedResult {
    entities: Vec::from(["m::A".to_string(), "m::B".to_string()]),
    completeness: "unavailable".to_string(),
    missing_relations: Vec::from(["LayoutDependency".to_string()])
  }
  affected_lane.completeness_info = completeness_info_subset("semantic-affected-closure",
    "relation families unavailable: LayoutDependency", 1, 2, 1)
  let with_analysis = PatchEvidenceBundle {
    affected: Option::Some(affected_lane.clone())
  }
  let carried_analysis = proof_patch_of_delta(&ChangeBudget {}, &semantic_delta_empty(),
    &proof_lane_evidence(), with_analysis)
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P11-analysis-completeness-attached",
    carried_analysis.analysis_completeness.len() == 1 &&
    carried_analysis.analysis_completeness[0] ==
      "semantic-affected-closure|conservative-subset|visited=1|returned=2|omitted=1|relation families unavailable: LayoutDependency")
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P11-analysis-completeness-defaulted-empty",
    proof_patch_new().analysis_completeness.len() == 0 &&
    proof_patch_of_delta(&ChangeBudget {}, &semantic_delta_empty(),
      &proof_lane_evidence()).analysis_completeness.len() == 0)

  # P12 (P0 proof-gating) — the truthful class ladder. A patch with a
  # Failed or Unavailable stage can NEVER construct VerifiedProofPatch;
  # each weaker class names exactly its own predicate.
  #   full_patch (P7)           — all fourteen Verified -> fully verified.
  #   gated_full                — compiler + budget Verified, equivalence
  #                               Unavailable -> budget-verified only.
  #   missing (P4)              — compiler Verified, budget Failed
  #                               (equivalence-required) -> compilation.
  #   route_patch (P7)          — post-mono Failed (captured, the shared
  #                               pipeline's checkpoint) + abi Failed ->
  #                               no class at all.
  #   failed_patch (P7)         — resolve Failed -> no class at all.
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P12-class-words",
    proof_patch_verified_class_word(full_patch.clone()) == "fully-verified" &&
    proof_patch_verified_class_word(gated_full.clone()) == "budget-verified" &&
    proof_patch_verified_class_word(missing.clone()) == "compilation-verified" &&
    proof_patch_verified_class_word(route_patch.clone()) == "unverified" &&
    proof_patch_verified_class_word(failed_patch.clone()) == "unverified")
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P12-predicates",
    proof_patch_compiler_verified(&full_patch) &&
    proof_patch_budget_verified(&full_patch) &&
    proof_patch_test_verified(&full_patch) &&
    proof_patch_all_verified(&full_patch) &&
    proof_patch_compiler_verified(&gated_full) &&
    proof_patch_budget_verified(&gated_full) &&
    !proof_patch_test_verified(&gated_full) &&
    proof_patch_compiler_verified(&missing) &&
    !proof_patch_budget_verified(&missing) &&
    !proof_patch_compiler_verified(&route_patch) &&
    !proof_patch_compiler_verified(&failed_patch))
  # A Failed/Unavailable stage cannot construct VerifiedProofPatch: the
  # route patch (Failed captured post-mono, Failed captured abi) and the
  # failed-evidence patch are both refused; the all-verified patch wraps.
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P12-failed-unavailable-cannot-wrap",
    verified_proof_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, route_patch.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none() &&
    verified_proof_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, failed_patch.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none() &&
    verified_proof_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, missing.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none() &&
    fully_verified_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, full_patch.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_some())
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P12-partial-classes",
    compilation_verified_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, missing.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_some() &&
    compilation_verified_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, route_patch.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none() &&
    compilation_verified_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFrontend, missing.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none() &&
    budget_verified_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, missing.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none() &&
    budget_verified_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, gated_full.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_some() &&
    test_verified_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, gated_full.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none() &&
    test_verified_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, full_patch.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_some())
  # An Unavailable delta (P9's status patch) refuses every class, and the
  # weaker classes are strictly weaker than the full one.
  proof_lane_expect(&mut out, "P12-unavailable-delta-refuses-every-class",
    compilation_verified_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, status_patch.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none() &&
    budget_verified_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, status_patch.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none() &&
    test_verified_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, status_patch.clone(), lane_hash.clone()).is_none() &&
    verified_proof_patch(VerificationLevel::VerifiedFull, status_patch, lane_hash.clone()).is_none())

  out
end
